.TH HTTP_RESPONSE_NEW 3
.SH NAME
http_response_new \- create a response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "http_response* http_response_new(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_response_new ()
allocates a response (cleared, code -1, content_length (uint64)-1, status 0) and puts it on top of
.IR h->response ;
the one that was there becomes
.IR next .
.BR http_open (3)
calls it, there is hardly a reason to do it by hand except in tests.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The response, or 0 if the memory is short.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_response_free(3), http_request_new(3)
